# Home: item → functionality / feature map (+ newState resource ids)

How each tool, quick action, widget and tile on `/home` links to `functionalitiesAccepted`, backend features and the newState ("What's New") resource id.
Sources: Channels.ApiGateway `Services/HomeBuilder/**` (incl. `*NewStateIndicator.cs`, `ExtensionMethods.cs`, `NewStateIndicatorDescriptionService.cs`, `Resources/Translations.resx`) and mysdworx-app `sd_feature_user/lib/src/constants.dart`, `sd_feature_home/.../get_home_data_usecase.dart`.
Related work items: US 1376859 (POC), US 1396315 (descriptions), US 1403124 (markasread), Task 1411432 (BE test).

Legend: **ALL** = every listed functionality is required. **ANY** = one is enough. BE = the backend only builds the item when this condition is met.

---

## 1. Tools (`tools[]`)

| Tool `type` | BE condition | newState resource | newState owner | Title / subtitle (EN) |
|--|--|--|--|--|
| `clocking` (ClockingTool) | feature `ClockingV2` enabled **AND** `sd://time/2.0.0/clocking` | `Tool:ClockingV2` | access right id | `New tool: Clocking` / `You now have access to your new tool.` |
| `aiHrAssistant` | access right with application code `Conversational employee` (AIAssistant). No functionality needed. | `Tool:AiHrAssistant` | **profile id** (GUID, `N` format, no dashes), not the access right | `New tool: Ai Hr Assistant` / same subtitle |

- Clocking **v1** is a different thing: the app shows the clocking component when `features[]` contains `Clocking` **and** a functionality has `sd://time/1.0.0/clocking`. When clocking v1 is present, the first tile is **not** moved into the "over animation" slot.

