## 5. newState mechanics (BE + app)

- The whole feature is gated by the pilot feature `PilotNewStateIndicator` on an access right, the `NewStateIndicator` config flag, and app version **≥ 5.5.0**.
- The very first home call for a profile marks the profile active. Everything existing at that moment is treated as already seen, so only items added afterwards are "new".
- Items stay new for at most 90 days (`NewStateVisibleForDays`).
- `isBrandNew` is true when **all** of the item's rows are unseen. `showCoachmark` is true when **any** unseen row hasn't been read yet.
- `markasseen` removes the indicator. `markasread` (US 1403124: "Ok, got it", Skip all, banner dismiss) removes the coachmark/banner but keeps the indicator.
- App coachmark order: **tools → quick actions → widgets → tiles**. The Webportal tile is always excluded. Coachmarks are only built from live API data, not from cache.
- App: if clocking v1 isn't active, the **first tile** in `tiles[]` is moved to the "over animation" slot. The Webportal tile is moved to its own web portal card.

